title: Support for the Government
subtitle: While PPS tolerates the cabinet from outside: end our support, or make a demand with or without a threat.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: parliament_affairs
card-image: img/polish/polish_government_support.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishGovernment.supportCardAvailable(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card parliament.government_support (technical reference 9.8; card catalogue 7.6). Since 0.64 only while PPS tolerates
// the cabinet; a PPS member has the card polish_coalition_affairs, which uses the options of this scene. An ordinary use
// costs this month's action once an option is confirmed and starts a 6-month renewal for this
// cabinet; opening and closing the card are free. Answers to a partner's warning or ultimatum use the
// pinned card polish_government_response for 0 T.
Q.pl_sup_mode = 'ordinary';
// Z — 0.56: why the card is in the deck now (half a year, or an act of the cabinet against PPS).
Q.pl_sup_reason = PolishGovernment.supportReason(Q);
Q.pl_sup_member = PolishGovernment.ppsStance(Q.S) === 'member' ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_sup_withdraw_reason = PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'withdraw', 'ordinary').reason;
Q.pl_sup_demand_reason = PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'bargain', 'ordinary').reason;
Q.pl_sup_military_reason = PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'bargain', 'ordinary', 'military_compromise').reason;
!}

= Our support for the government

[? if pl_sup_reason : [+ pl_sup_reason +] ?]

Prime minister: [+ prime_minister_display +]. PPS position: [+ pps_government_position +].

[? if pl_cabinet_support_display : Declared support: [+ pl_cabinet_support_display +]. ?]

**End our support** takes effect at once; in the same sequence PPS decides whether to support a motion to dismiss the cabinet. **A threat** makes our demand a condition of further support: if the government refuses, we must either carry the threat out or back down. **Persuasion** asks without a threat and costs no relations.

- @withdraw
- @bargain
- @persuade
- @bargain_military
- @persuade_military
- @easy_discard

@withdraw
title: [? if pl_sup_member : Leave the cabinet with our ministers ?][? if not pl_sup_member : End our support of the cabinet ?]
subtitle: [? if pl_sup_member : Our ministers resign and our coalition agreements end. ?][? if not pl_sup_member : Our agreements with the cabinet end. ?] The cabinet continues as a minority government unless the Sejm dismisses it.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'withdraw', Q.pl_sup_mode).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_sup_withdraw_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
var left = PolishGovernment.withdrawSupport(Q, Q.pl_sup_mode);
Q.pl_sup_fell = left.fell ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: motion if not pl_sup_fell; fallen if pl_sup_fell

@bargain
title: [? if pl_sup_member : Put financed worker protection to the Council of Ministers, or we leave the cabinet ?][? if not pl_sup_member : Demand financed worker protection, or we end our support ?]
subtitle: [? if pl_sup_member : Our coalition partners weigh how much they need us. ?][? if not pl_sup_member : The government weighs how much it needs us. ?] Parties that give in under a threat think less of us (−3 relation).
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'bargain', Q.pl_sup_mode).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_sup_demand_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
Q.pl_sup_postulate = 'worker_protection';
var record = PolishGovernment.supportDemand(Q, 'bargain', 'worker_protection', Q.pl_sup_mode);
Q.pl_sup_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_sup_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
!}
go-to: demand_result if pl_sup_accepted; threat if not pl_sup_accepted

@persuade
title: [? if pl_sup_member : Propose financed worker protection in the Council of Ministers, without a threat ?][? if not pl_sup_member : Ask for financed worker protection, without a threat ?]
subtitle: No threat, no relation change either way; [? if pl_sup_member : if refused, we stay in the cabinet as before. ?][? if not pl_sup_member : if refused, our support stays as it is. ?]
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'persuade', Q.pl_sup_mode).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_sup_demand_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
Q.pl_sup_postulate = 'worker_protection';
var record = PolishGovernment.supportDemand(Q, 'persuade', 'worker_protection', Q.pl_sup_mode);
Q.pl_sup_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_sup_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
!}
go-to: demand_result

@bargain_military
view-if: {! return PolishGovernment.militaryCaseOpen(Q) !}
title: [? if pl_sup_member : Demand a compromise with Piłsudski under civilian control, or we leave the cabinet ?][? if not pl_sup_member : Demand a compromise with Piłsudski under civilian control, or we end our support ?]
subtitle: The cabinet carries it out itself at its next review, if Piłsudski accepts a military function under civilian control. Parties that give in under a threat think less of us (−3 relation).
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'bargain', Q.pl_sup_mode, 'military_compromise').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_sup_military_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
Q.pl_sup_postulate = 'military_compromise';
var record = PolishGovernment.supportDemand(Q, 'bargain', 'military_compromise', Q.pl_sup_mode);
Q.pl_sup_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_sup_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
!}
go-to: demand_result if pl_sup_accepted; threat if not pl_sup_accepted

@persuade_military
view-if: {! return PolishGovernment.militaryCaseOpen(Q) !}
title: [? if pl_sup_member : Propose a compromise with Piłsudski in the Council of Ministers, without a threat ?][? if not pl_sup_member : Ask the cabinet for a compromise with Piłsudski, without a threat ?]
subtitle: The cabinet carries it out itself at its next review, if Piłsudski accepts. No threat and no relation change either way.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'persuade', Q.pl_sup_mode, 'military_compromise').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_sup_military_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
Q.pl_sup_postulate = 'military_compromise';
var record = PolishGovernment.supportDemand(Q, 'persuade', 'military_compromise', Q.pl_sup_mode);
Q.pl_sup_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_sup_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
!}
go-to: demand_result

@maintain
title: [? if pl_sup_member : Stay in the cabinet as before ?][? if not pl_sup_member : Keep our support as it is ?]
subtitle: [? if pl_resp_kind = "review" : The toleration goes on to the end of its six months. ?][? if pl_resp_kind = "renewal" : The toleration is renewed for six months, with a new review after three. ?][? if pl_resp_kind != "review" and pl_resp_kind != "renewal" : No new condition. The broken promise stays broken; the partner's case remains open. ?]
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'maintain', Q.pl_sup_mode).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: Only as an answer to a partner's warning or ultimatum.
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.maintainSupport(Q);
!}
go-to: maintained

@extension
title: Ask the partner for three more months
subtitle: One standard extension of the overdue promise, if the partner accepts; it records the new date, not progress.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'extension', Q.pl_sup_mode).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_sup_extension_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
var record = PolishGovernment.requestExtension(Q);
Q.pl_sup_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_sup_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
!}
go-to: extension_result

@threat
new-page: true

= [? if pl_sup_member : Our coalition partners refuse ?][? if not pl_sup_member : The government refuses ?]

[+ pl_sup_answers +]

A threat must be real. We decide now, without spending another month.

- @carry_out
- @back_down

@carry_out
title: [? if pl_sup_member : Carry out the threat: leave the cabinet ?][? if not pl_sup_member : Carry out the threat: end our support ?]
subtitle: [? if pl_sup_member : The ordinary effects of leaving the cabinet, ?][? if not pl_sup_member : The ordinary effects of ending our support, ?] including the decision on a motion to dismiss the cabinet.
on-arrival: {!
var result = PolishGovernment.answerThreat(Q, 'carry_out');
Q.pl_sup_fell = result.fell ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: motion if not pl_sup_fell; fallen if pl_sup_fell

@back_down
title: Back down
subtitle: Our reputation for keeping our word falls (−5); later threats against this cabinet count only as persuasion.
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.answerThreat(Q, 'back_down');
!}
go-to: backed_down

@backed_down
new-page: true

= We back down

[? if pl_sup_member : PPS stays in the cabinet without the concession. ?][? if not pl_sup_member : PPS keeps supporting the cabinet without the concession. ?] The government will not take our next threat seriously while this cabinet lasts.

- @root: Continue.

@demand_result
new-page: true

= The answer

[+ pl_sup_answers +]

[? if pl_sup_accepted and pl_sup_postulate = "worker_protection" : **The government accepts.** Financed worker protection enters our agreement with the cabinet, due within four months. ?]

[? if pl_sup_accepted and pl_sup_postulate = "military_compromise" : **The government accepts.** The compromise enters our agreement with the cabinet. The cabinet offers Piłsudski a military function under civilian control at its next review; if he refuses, the promise lapses without a breach. ?]

[? if not pl_sup_accepted and pl_sup_member : **Our coalition partners refuse.** We stay in the cabinet as before. ?]

[? if not pl_sup_accepted and not pl_sup_member : **The government refuses.** Our support stays as it was. ?]

- @root: Continue.

@extension_result
new-page: true

= The answer

[+ pl_sup_answers +]

[? if pl_sup_accepted : **The partner accepts three more months.** The promise keeps its content; its new date is recorded, and the ultimatum ends if nothing else is overdue. ?]

[? if not pl_sup_accepted : **The partner refuses.** The ultimatum stands. ?]

- @root: Continue.

@maintained
new-page: true

= [? if pl_sup_member : We stay in the cabinet ?][? if not pl_sup_member : We keep our support ?]

[? if pl_resp_kind = "review" : Our toleration goes on as agreed until the end of its six months. ?][? if pl_resp_kind = "renewal" : Our toleration is renewed for six months; its next review comes after three. ?][? if pl_resp_kind != "review" and pl_resp_kind != "renewal" : Nothing changes in our agreement. The partner still waits for the promise. ?]

- @root: Continue.

@motion
new-page: true
call: polish_opening_state
on-arrival: {!
Q.pl_sup_motion_reason = PolishGovernment.dismissalSupportStatus(Q).reason;
!}

= [? if pl_sup_member : We have left the cabinet ?][? if not pl_sup_member : Our support has ended ?]

[+ pl_cabinet_support_display +]. Without us the cabinet governs as a minority unless the Sejm dismisses it. A motion to dismiss the cabinet is now possible; the votes of the clubs decide it.

- @own_motion_support
- @own_motion_refuse

@own_motion_support
title: Support the motion to dismiss the cabinet
subtitle: The motion passes if more MPs vote for it than against, with at least 148 present.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.dismissalSupportStatus(Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_sup_motion_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.decideDismissal(Q, 'support');
!}
go-to: vote_result

@own_motion_refuse
title: Do not take part in bringing the cabinet down
subtitle: PPS abstains; the motion is still voted on.
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.decideDismissal(Q, 'refuse');
!}
go-to: vote_result

@vote_result
new-page: true
call: polish_opening_state

= The vote

[+ pl_last_dismissal_display +]

[? if pl_last_dismissal_passed : **The cabinet is dismissed.** It stays as caretaker until the head of state appoints a new one; the formation of a new cabinet follows. No election is called. ?]

[? if not pl_last_dismissal_passed : **The cabinet survives** as a minority government. ?]

- @root: Continue.

@fallen
new-page: true
call: polish_opening_state

= The cabinet resigns

The prime minister's own party has left the cabinet, so the cabinet resigns. It stays as caretaker until the head of state appoints a new one; the formation of a new cabinet follows. No election is called.

- @root: Continue.
